ous how no you know no nonsense and  and just incredibly strong um and yet  obviously incredibly flawed uh which was  a wonderful journeys character she got  through to that side of lou that um  she doesn't often show she's a woman who  works by herself and and resents having  to work with with with um journey's  character um  just the the exploration of these two  women and their different paths in life  and and their judgment of each other and  ultimate respect for each other was a  great um story to tell to be honest with  you the reason i wanted to cover this  junket is because i'm a big fan of your  work allison and i want to see more  women kicking ass in these kinds of  roles so i'm happy to talk to you guys  about it um do you have a newfound  respect for like liam neeson and what he  did with the taken movies after doing  the physicality of this film yes i do i  really do i don't know how old liam was  when he started doing those taken films  but i you know uh at 61 it was a huge it  was incredible thing to to to to  challenge myself with and and the  physicality i was scared i was you know  i'm not gonna lie i did a lot of  training but i was also like please oh  god please don't let me i i just didn't  want to hurt myself and not be able to  do the get through the film and and um  and i i didn't i i thank the daniel  bernhard our you know the choreographer  who made it safe for us in all those  fights i knew exactly where he was and  where his arm was coming and what you  know that was all worked out so  specifically and um technically that it  made it almost impossible for for for us  to hurt ourselves and that was um great  and and we just felt protected on set by  the crew by our director anna we we  we felt it was a safe environment to  take chances physically for both of you  when i was watching the film i know how  films are made and the long hours and  when you're filming on location like you  did for this film it's it's a challenge  um so for both